From 2f7c0e4a891f9e7e37302830cae058baa0e80719 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Basanagouda Nagappa Koppad <basanagouda.nagappa.koppad@intel.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 02:43:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] drm: Add CRTC color adjustment

Port of the Intel drm-hwcomposer fork commit 57d6bca ("Add display
color adjustment function"), enabled with
vendor.hwcomposer.color.adjustment.enabling=1.

Values are read from /data/vendor/color/ when the display is powered
on:
 - hue (0..359) and saturation (75..125 %) build a BT.709 hue/saturation
   matrix that is multiplied into the CRTC CTM after the SurfaceFlinger
   color transform. The fork set the CTM out of band with
   drmModeObjectSetProperty, which the per-frame atomic CTM would
   override.
 - brightness and contrast (0..255, 128 neutral) build a CRTC GAMMA_LUT
   that is set in the atomic commit. Neutral values give an identity
   LUT (sampled over 0..lut_size-1, brightness centred on 128).

Non-finite values (nan, inf) in the color files are ignored, like
unreadable or out-of-range ones.

Disabled by default; the GAMMA_LUT properties are only looked up when
the feature is enabled.

Tracked-On: NIACP3-1589
Signed-off-by: Basanagouda Nagappa Koppad <basanagouda.nagappa.koppad@intel.com>
